.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-LOADTEST 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-loadtest
.Nd load the network, the disks and process creation at once, so every dashboard has something to show
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar seconds
.Op Fl -http-only | -io-only | -fork-only
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
For a live demonstration: run
.Nm
in one terminal and walk through the eBPF views, the TCP details and the
Grafana dashboards while every layer is busy.
For
.Ar seconds ,
60 by default, it runs at once:
.Bl -tag -width "process"
.It HTTP
50 connections against the demo deployment in the cluster, deployed
first if missing, which Hubble, Cilium's load balancer and conntrack show.
.It Disk
.Xr fio 1
reading and writing a 2 GB file in
.Pa /var/tmp ,
which moves the ZFS transaction groups, the ARC and the block-latency
heat map.
.It Processes
a loop starting short-lived processes, which Tetragon's exec rate shows.
.El
.Pp
It removes what it started \(em the pods, fio, the loop, the file \(em
when it ends or is interrupted.
The arguments may come in either order.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -http-only , Fl -io-only , Fl -fork-only
Only that layer.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the header comment and exit 0, starting nothing.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when it ran; 2 when an argument is neither a number of seconds nor a
layer.
.Sh EXAMPLES
On a kldload desktop on 2026-09-30, with this release's
.Nm
first on the path:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kldload-loadtest abc
kldload-loadtest: not a number of seconds or a mode: abc (see --help)
# (exited 2)
.Ed
.Pp
Running it; not done for this page:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kldload-loadtest 120
# kldload-loadtest --io-only 30
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fio 1 ,
.Xr kldload-dash 8 ,
.Xr kube-demo 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-30, writing this page:
.Ql kldload-loadtest --io-only
read the layer as the number of seconds and ran all three.
Earlier the same day,
.Fl -help
started a load test.
